{"type":"thinking","text":"I have a good understanding of the workflow. The parent fan-out invokes `fanout-run.cjs` which runs each lineage. The lineage dirs (locks, ledgers, containment baseline, .executor-state) were pre-created. I need to run:\n\nphase_init:\n- directories prompt, iterations, deltas\n- create config (with topic, session ID `fanout-dsh-live-1793980580137-7tzq73`, maxIterations 1, convergence threshold 0.05, antiConvergence minIterations 3 (will clamp to 1), stopPolicy convergence, specFolder, resource_map false)\n- create state log via gateway run_initialized\n- create strategy\n- create registry\n- maybe dashboard? The workflow doesn't explicitly create dashboard at init; reducer generates it after iteration. But phase_init complete perhaps doesn't create dashboard. The dashboard is reducer-owned and will be generated by reduce-state after iteration. Fine.\n- lock acquisition? The fan-out runner may have acquired? There is `locks-and-fencing-v1` with a hash dir. Maybe fanout-run acquired a lock. Hmm, need to check. The lineage dir has `locks-and-fencing-v1/218eeb...` with maybe files. Let me inspect.\n\nAlso note `state_paths` per config: config at `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json`, strategy etc. The prompt pack uses `research/...` placeholders in the template but the actual paths from state_paths are lineage dir paths. Since I'm not rendering a prompt file for dispatch (I run inline), I may still need to create `prompts/iteration-001.md`? The post_dispatch_validate checks iteration file, state record, route proof, delta file. It doesn't check prompt file. The task says \"treat executor-dispatch steps as done\". I could write the prompt for completeness, but it's not required by the completion line? The task says \"Run phase_init, phase_main_loop (to legal convergence OR config.maxIterations, whichever comes first), and phase_synthesis.\" The prompt pack is part of dispatch. I might create it to be faithful, but it's extra work and write surface is fine. Let's focus on required artifacts.\n\nThe verification step uses `verify-iteration.cjs --loop-type research --artifact-dir <artifact_dir> --iteration 1`. That's a repo script writing? It might write dispatch receipts? It reads. It may be safe (only reads). But the instruction says don't run repo tooling like validate.sh --recursive, generate-context.js, git writes. The gateway and reducer are explicitly required. verify-iteration should be okay but maybe it writes state log? Let me check the script quickly. Actually the reducer and gateway are required; verify-iteration is a mechanical gate, can run read-only likely. But perhaps it requires dispatch receipts. Let me inspect.\n\nAlso the append gateway requires a run authority record. `deep_research.run_initialized` creates it. Need to ensure event file format: stem/scope/data. The workflow provides exact command. I can adapt paths.\n\nNow, the research itself. Topic: \"What do the two checked-in DeepSeek Harness route patches under .dsh/patches/ declare (endpoint, model id, reasoning effort, compat flags), and do they agree with each other? Read the files; answer in under 200 words.\"\n\nI have read both patches. Need to research and produce findings with citations:\n- route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml: provider llmgateway, displayName LLM Gateway, apiKeyEnv LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY, api openai-completions, baseURL https://api.llmgateway.io/v1, compat thinkingFormat: deepseek, supportsDeveloperRole: false, models: id deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, name DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, reasoningEfforts off: / high: high / max: max; agent-default-model provider llmgateway, model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, reasoningEffort max.\n- route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml: provider opencode-go, displayName OpenCode Go, apiKeyEnv OPENCODE_API_KEY, api openai-completions, baseURL https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1, compat same, models: id deepseek-v4.1-flash (no -1017), name DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, reasoningEfforts same; agent-default-model provider opencode-go, model deepseek-v4.1-flash, reasoningEffort max.\n- Agreement: same API shape, compat flags (thinkingFormat deepseek, supportsDeveloperRole false), same effort ladder and default max; differ in endpoint, key env var, provider id, and model id (snapshot-suffixed vs base id). Both target DeepSeek V4.1 Flash.\n- The opencode-go patch's own comment says \"the endpoint is unverified until a keyed run proves it.\" So they don't fully agree on model id and endpoint; one is pinned snapshot, other base id; they agree on compat/reasoning.\n\nAlso worth checking references in the repo that name these model ids and endpoints (e.g., executor-config.ts allowlist, packet docs). The research topic says \"Read the files; answer in under 200 words.\" So primarily the two patch files. I can add cross-checks in packet docs for agreement/verification. But since maxIterations=1 and under 200 words, keep it focused.\n\nThe completion criteria in the prompt (phase 13 overall) are for the operator packet, not this research lineage. My mandate is the research topic only. The lineage completion line is the only output. But maybe I should consider completion criteria? The dispatched worker prompt says research topic. The Goal section at top describes the phase's overall objective; the lineage is one part. My write surface is only the lineage. I should not try to satisfy the whole phase completion criteria (evidence/, executor-config.ts) because that's outside my write authority. The research topic is narrow.\n\nWait — the \"Goal: Phase 13: dsh-live-contract-pin\" then \"Session Context\" and the dispatched worker prompt. The task is to orchestrate the deep-research workflow as a detached fan-out lineage. So yes, my job is the research lineage only; the parent merges lineages and later the phase work happens. I must not modify outside the lineage.\n\nNow, read steer.md — doesn't exist. Good.\n\nBefore writing, I need Gate 5: REPO RULES.md load. The first write is upcoming. Let me read REPO RULES.md and identify trigger table. Also Gate 1 trigger index lookup. Let me do these quickly, though this is a child dispatch. The system prompt insists.\n\nActually, consideration: The child-dispatch exemption says \"Law 4, Halt Conditions, Logic-Sync, Escalation and stop-for-yes are record-and-continue; acting outside it is barred.\" It doesn't exempt Gate 5. Gate 5 binds first write in a repo with REPO RULES.md. So read REPO RULES.md and load matched rules. Let me do that. Also Gate 1 lookup — before any tool per instructions; I already used tools, but I can run it now before writes. It's read-only and may produce noisy output. Let me run with `--scoring-only --json` and short prompt. It's required. I'll treat failure as clean no-hit.\n\nGate 2: The user named deep-research skill (the prompt directly says read SKILL.md and execute). I can cite \"User specified: ...\". The skill catalog deep-research matches. I have loaded the SKILL.md directly; calling skill tool would duplicate. The instruction says \"If the user names a skill... call the skill tool with the exact skill name before taking task actions.\" I haven't. Should I call it? It may return the same SKILL.md content (already in context). The task explicitly instructs reading the file, which I did. I'll note user directed. To be safe, I could call `skill` with `deep-research` — but that adds a large duplicate. The rule says \"A skill already in context is not re-read\" (Gate 5 loading rule applies to routing). I'll consider it loaded via the file read.\n\nLet me read REPO RULES.md now and run Gate 1 lookup in parallel. Also inspect gateway/reducer scripts and lock state. Let me batch.\n\nAlso, I want to see the `fanout-run.cjs` invocation metadata for this lineage to know exactly what env and args were used. `.executor-state` may have a file. Let me list it and read. Also locks-and-fencing-v1 content.\n\nLet me run a batch:\n1. read REPO RULES.md (read tool)\n2. bash lookup-trigger-index (may take)\n3. bash inspect .executor-state, locks, ledgers, containment baseline root files\n4. bash inspect gateway usage/help and reduce-state; verify-iteration.\n\nLet's do it."}
