ness\",\n       \"model\": \"deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017\",\n       \"reasoningEffort\": \"max\",\n       \"serviceTier\": null,\n       \"sandboxMode\": \"workspace-write\",\n       \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n     }\n     ```\n     Note executor-config.ts may expect `type` rather than `kind`? In the YAML it says `resolve_executor.source: config.executor` and branches `config.executor.type`. But the template uses `\"kind\": \"native\"`. Hmm. The executor config parser likely normalizes. For fanout lineages, the config is expected to include executor block. Let me check executor-config.ts parseExecutorConfig for accepted shape and kind names. Also `executor-config.ts` is in the phase completion criteria (allowlist). But I only need config shape.\n\n3. `lineage`: sessionId, parentSessionId null, lineageMode new, generation 1, continuedFromRun null. Also maybe `fanout`: not necessary; the lineage is one.\n4. `nextRunAt`, `remainingDelayMs` null.\n5. `resource_map_present`: false, `resource_map`: {\"emit\": true?} Wait `step_create_config` populates `resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"` where default true; but step_emit_resource_map uses config.resource_map.emit. I can set true. But emitting resource-map requires deltas with sources; my delta will have sources. Fine, but not required by completion criteria? The skill success criteria says resource-map.md produced unless config.resource_map.emit == false. I'll set emit true and produce it? The phase_synthesis step_emit_resource_map command writes `{state_paths.resource_map_output}` via reducer with `--emit-resource-map`. That writes inside lineage dir, okay. But it reads deltas and writes resource-map. It may also need the config `resource_map_present`. Let's do it faithfully. Or set emit false to avoid extra complexity. The task doesn't require resource map. But the workflow says emit unless false. Since defaults true, I'd run it. The reducer command with `--emit-resource-map` likely writes resource-map.md in artifact