ion gate might check the ledger's last run. Let me test later.\n\nActually, the synthesis closeout is part of the workflow and has been used; it must work. The scope run ID might be resolved by `basename(dirname(stateLog))` = \"dsh-live\", and the gateway may allow any run because the run authority is keyed by the ledger, not the scope. Or the closeout may be failing silently? We'll see. If refused, I'll need to construct the synthesis event manually with the correct scope (session id) and submit via gateway. That's allowed: the task says hand every state record to the gateway exactly as the YAML runs it. The YAML uses closeout; but if it fails, I can adapt. First try the standard command.\n\nAlso, the closeout event names: `synthesis_complete` stem `deep_research.synthesis_complete`. The gateway upcaster must know this stem. It likely does.\n\nThe state log projection after gateway: does it include the run_initialized and iteration rows? The gateway refreshes from ledger. The projection may contain all canonical events. The verify-iteration reads the state log and delta. It will find the iteration record in the projection if the gateway wrote it.\n\nLet me inspect the gateway's main loop briefly to know event handling and scope checks. Search for `run_initialized`, `scope`, `authority`, `stable-identity`."}
