ance: both define the same patch IDs and providers but different provider maps; applying both sequentially would overwrite the first provider? Actually each patch adds a provider under `providers` and sets `agent-default-model`. If applied both, the second may add its provider while keeping the first? The patch system maybe merges by id. But both target `llm-pi-ai` and `agent-default-model`; the second would override. They are alternatives. The research answer should say they are two mutually exclusive route choices, sharing compat/reasoning, differing in endpoint, provider id, key var, and model id.\n\nLet me read `.dsh/README.md` and `SYNC.md` relevant lines, and check the original 004 evidence files. Then I have enough for the iteration.\n\nAlso, the goal prompt mentions \"do they agree with each other?\" This is a factual question, not judgment. No need for a second lens.\n\nLet me read these docs."}
