{"type":"tool_result","callId":"call_00_9VPnGCgJMxq3NImTfaMa3231","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.dsh/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n16: \n17: `dsh` reads this folder only when a dispatch names its files with `--patch`. A dispatch passes exactly one route patch, the lineage patch and the guards patch. The route patch picks the provider and model. The lineage patch turns off telemetry export, the DeepSeek session log, goal rounds and plan mode.\n18: \n19: The `cli-deepseek-harness` mode packet under `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/` owns the dispatch contract and its hard rules. [SYNC.md](./SYNC.md) owns the inventory and the drift check.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 2. STRUCTURE\n24: \n25: | Path | Purpose |\n26: |---|---|\n27: | `patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` | Routes to LLM Gateway, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, key variable `LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY` |\n28: | `patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` | Routes to OpenCode Go, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, key variable `OPENCODE_API_KEY`. Endpoint unverified |\n29: | `patches/lineage.patch.yml` | Disables telemetry export, `session-log-deepseek`, `goal-round-driver`, `command-goal` and `plan-mode` |\n30: | `patches/guards.patch.yml` | Loads the required repo-guards plugin for every dispatch |\n31: | `plugins/repo-guards/` | Guard adapters and tests, activated by `patches/guards.patch.yml` |\n32: | `skills/` | Generated relative symlinks, one per canonical skill, which dsh discovers natively |\n33: | `prompts/` | Generated pointer stubs, one per command, composed into a dispatch's task text |\n34: | `agents/` | Generated persona patches, passed as `--patch .dsh/agents/<name>.patch.yml` |\n35: | `SYNC.md` | Surface inventory, generators, what stays out of this folder and the drift checks |\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. USAGE EXAMPLES\n40: \n41: Run from a temp working directory with a disposable home, never from the repository root:\n42: \n43: ```bash\n44: REPO=\"$(pwd -P)\"\n45: H=$(mktemp -d); W=$(mktemp -d)\n46: cd \"$W\" && printf 'Reply with the single word OK' | DSH_HOME=\"$H\" dsh --profile headless \\\n47:   --patch \"$REPO/.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\" \\\n48:   --patch \"$REPO/.dsh/patches/lineage.patch.yml\" \\\n49:   --patch \"$REPO/.dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml\" \\\n50:   --json --permission-mode read-only --approval-policy never -\n51: ```\n52: \n53: The last stdout line is a `final` event. Exit 0 with `final.reason.kind` `completed` is success. With no key in the environment the run exits 1 and the `final` event carries `MISSING_CREDENTIAL` for the named route.\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 4. RELATED RESOURCES\n58: \n59: - [SYNC.md](./SYNC.md): surface inventory and drift check.\n60: - `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-deepseek-harness/`: the mode packet and its hard rules.\n\n(End of file - total 60 lines)\n</content>"}
{"type":"tool_result","callId":"call_01_v9LXRJridFMeQexBjxg47446","status":"completed","result":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.dsh/SYNC.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n15: \n16: This folder holds the `--patch` layers the repository owns. Model selection belongs to the harness, so the closed roster is enforced here: one route patch per roster entry, and a lineage patch that switches off every surface a non-interactive dispatch must not run. The base default route is the official DeepSeek API, and a dispatch that names no route patch falls through to it.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. SURFACE INVENTORY\n21: \n22: | Surface | Mechanism | Source | Can it drift? |\n23: |---|---|---|---|\n24: | `patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** route patch | none | Yes. `--dump-config` shows the composed `llm-pi-ai` provider and the `agent-default-model` row |\n25: | `patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** route patch | none | Yes, same check. Its endpoint is unverified until a keyed run proves it |\n26: | `patches/lineage.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** lineage patch | none | Yes. `--dump-config` shows telemetry `DISABLED` and the four disabled rows |\n27: | `patches/guards.patch.yml` | **hand-authored** patch that inserts the `repo-guards` row | none | Yes. A keyless boot with it must print no `did not activate` line |\n28: | `patches/mcp-code-mode.patch.yml` | **hand-authored**, opt-in patch that mounts one `code_mode` stdio server | `.pi/mcp.json` | Yes. A keyless boot with it must leave no new `mcp-code-mode-launcher` process |\n29: | `plugins/repo-guards/` | **hand-authored** plugin bundle; its adapters call the shared guard cores under `.skilled/` | `.skilled/hooks/`, `.skilled/skills/*/runtime/hooks/` | Yes. `node --test .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/tests/` |\n30: | `skills/<name>` | **generated** relative symlink, one per canonical `SKILL.md`, named by its frontmatter `name` | `.skilled/skills/**/SKILL.md` | Yes. `sync-skills-dsh.cjs --check` |\n31: | `prompts/*.md` | **generated** pointer stubs | `.skilled/commands/**/*.md` | Yes. `sync-prompts-dsh.cjs --check` |\n32: | `agents/<name>.patch.yml` | **generated** persona patch, one `system-prompt` row whose `personaPrefix` is the agent body | `.skilled/agents/*.md` | Yes. `sync-agents-dsh.cjs --check` |\n33: | `README.md` | hand-authored | none | No |\n34: | `SYNC.md` | hand-authored | none | No |\n35: \n36: ### Repo-guards adapters\n37: \n38: | Adapter | DSH event | Scope | Error policy |\n39: |---|---|---|---|\n\n(Showing lines 15-39 of 124. Use offset=40 to continue.)\n</content>"}
