{"type":"thinking","text":"Excellent. Now I have strong corroboration from prior evidence:\n- `.dsh/README.md:17` says a dispatch passes exactly one route patch. This is key: the two route patches are alternatives, not applied together.\n- `.dsh/README.md:27-28` lists both and notes opencode-go endpoint unverified.\n- `.dsh/SYNC.md:24-25` confirms both hand-authored route patches, `--dump-config` verified, opencode-go endpoint unverified until keyed run.\n- `004.../evidence/dump-config-*.txt` show composed config matches patches (provider/model/effort/baseURL/compat). This is a second source proving the patches' declarations. Great.\n\nNow, do they agree?\n- Same: API `openai-completions`; compat `thinkingFormat: deepseek`, `supportsDeveloperRole: false`; reasoning ladder `off`, `high: high`, `max: max`; default `reasoningEffort: max`; same display name \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\"; same patch target ids `llm-pi-ai` and `agent-default-model`.\n- Differ: provider id (`llmgateway` vs `opencode-go`), display name, key env (`LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY` vs `OPENCODE_API_KEY`), baseURL (`https://api.llmgateway.io/v1` vs `https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1`), model id (`deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` vs `deepseek-v4.1-flash`).\n- The opencode-go patch self-declares endpoint unverified until a keyed run proves it (lines 1-2). The llmgateway patch does not carry that caveat.\n- They are mutually exclusive per dispatch: README says exactly one route patch (line 17), and both patch the same rows `llm-pi-ai` and `agent-default-model`.\n\nThis is a crisp answer under 200 words.\n\nNow, the research process actions:\n1. Read `.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:1-24`\n2. Read `.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml:1-25`\n3. Read `.dsh/README.md:17,27-28` and `.dsh/SYNC.md:24-25`\n4. Read prior packet evidence `dump-config-llmgateway.txt:60-62,95-100` and `dump-config-opencode-go.txt:60-62,95-100`\nThat's 4-6 research actions (within 3-5 target; maybe 6 files). Good.\n\nNow let's think about newInfoRatio. Since this is iteration 1 of 1, all findings are new relative to the lineage. newInfoRatio = 1.0? The formula: fully new findings count 1.0, no partially new. So 1.0. But convergence threshold 0.05; 1.0 > 0.05, so no convergence; maxIterations 1 stops. That's fine. The status should be `complete` (normal evidence gathering) or `insight`. `complete` is right.\n\nfindingsCount: let's define 5 findings:\n1. `llmgateway` route declares LLM Gateway endpoint `https://api.llmgateway.io/v1`, `openai-completions`, key `LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY`, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, effort `max`.\n2. `opencode-go` route declares OpenCode Go endpoint `https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1`, `openai-completions`, key `OPENCODE_API_KEY`, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, effort `max`.\n3. Both declare identical compat: `thinkingFormat: deepseek`, `supportsDeveloperRole: false`, and the same effort ladder (off/high/max) with default max.\n4. The routes differ in provider id, endpoint, key env, and exact model id; the opencode-go patch itself marks the endpoint unverified until a keyed run proves it.\n5. They are alternative pins, not additive: each targets the same patch rows `llm-pi-ai`/`agent-default-model`, and the repo README says a dispatch passes exactly one route patch; prior `--dump-config` evidence confirms each composed route separately.\nMaybe 6: model ids both map to the same \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\" display name and both are within the DSH roster; `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` is the DSH default. But 5 is enough.\n\nThe delta's finding rows must have `\"label\"` (the finding text), `\"id\"`, `\"iteration\":1`, `\"sources\":[...]`. The verify-iteration counts delta rows with `hasReadableFindingText` (label). It counts 5 if I include 5 finding rows. The markdown count under `## Findings` must be 5, and graph count 0 (or omit graphEvents). The record's `findingsCount` = 5. The verifier requires all three equal [markdownCount, graphCount, deltaCount]? Let me inspect the comparison logic to ensure it allows 5,0,5 (i.e., it checks each count equals claimed?). Let me read around line 448-466."}
