{"type":"thinking","text":"The gateway will create `deep-research-ledger/frames` under the run directory (artifact dir). Good. The `checkGatewayReceipt` uses `path.dirname(artifactDir)` as artifact root; for lineage dir, that's `.../lineages`, and the projection relativePath likely `dsh-live/deep-research-state.jsonl`; the watermark dir under `lineages/.legacy-projection-watermarks`. Hmm. The gateway might use `--run-directory` artifact dir; the authority watermark may be elsewhere. The verifier's gateway receipt check is only enabled if env `DEEP_LOOP_VERIFY_GATEWAY_RECEIPT=1`; default skipped. The ledger backing check calls `checkGatewayReceipt`; if it returns `not-enforced` or `skipped`, then `checkLedgerBacking` returns not-enforced (not unbacked). So no failure. Good.\n\nThe gateway writes `deep-research-ledger` under the run directory (artifact dir) as per the verifier comment. Fine.\n\n### Config path and reducer artifact dir\nThe reducer command takes `<spec_folder> --artifact-dir <lineage_dir>`. It resolves relative paths. Run from repo root:\n`node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs specs/.../013-dsh-live-contract-pin --artifact-dir specs/.../lineages/dsh-live`\n\nIt writes resource map etc. Good.\n\n### The DSH session's own memory / tool\nI must not use the `skill` tool? It's not a nested CLI; it's a tool. The prompt says no nested CLI/agent/subprocess to run an iteration. Using `read`/`write`/`bash` is fine. Running repo scripts (gateway, reducer) is required.\n\n### Time\nLet me capture the clock and start writing. Before that, let me create a todo list for the work (multi-step). The tool is available; useful. Let me set up todos.\n\nThen:\n1. Create directories.\n2. Write config.\n3. Run step_create_state_log via gateway.\n4. Write strategy.\n5. Write registry.\n6. (Optional lock)\n7. Write iteration file.\n8. Write delta.\n9. Append iteration record via gateway.\n10. Run reducer.\n11. Run verify-iteration.\n12. Write research.md.\n13. Run resource map emission.\n14. Run synthesis closeout + gateway.\n15. Update config status complete.\n16. Verify final state; print completion line.\n\nNote the closeout requires registry findings; reducer writes registry. Good.\n\nOne concern: The config's `specFolder` should be the packet spec folder (relative path), and `artifact_dir` is the lineage dir. The reducer uses `resolveArtifactRoot` if `--artifact-dir` absent; we pass it. The `researchDir` = artifact_dir. The `specFolder` is used for packet context, not for writes. Fine.\n\nAnother concern: `step_create_state_log` gateway event requires the config file to exist and the authority to be open. The fanout effect ledger's grant journal shows a lease that expired at 15:57; the current time is ~16:56. The authority may be \"legacy_authoritative\" and open. The gateway might see the effect intent but not a run. Let's test.\n\nLet me first capture the current UTC time and create the directories/config. I'll use the `write` tool for the config (after constructing JSON). But I need the timestamp first. Let me run `date -u`. Also check `DSH_HOME` env (do not read keys) to confirm it's a temp dir. `env | grep DSH_HOME` is safe (no key). The instruction says never read/copy/print a key. Checking DSH_HOME is fine. But not necessary.\n\nLet me create a todo list and then the directories."}
