{"type":"thinking","text":"Now the delta. Need the canonical iteration record as line 1, then 5 finding rows. Let me construct with a Node script to ensure valid JSON, using the config session ID, timestamp, duration. I'll write `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` via Node (fs.writeFileSync) from repo root, with paths. The fields:\n\n```\n{\n  \"type\":\"iteration\",\n  \"iteration\":1,\n  \"run\":1,\n  \"runId\":\"fanout-dsh-live-...\",\n  \"sessionId\":\"...\",\n  \"lineageId\":\"...\",\n  \"mode\":\"research\",\n  \"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\n  \"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\n  \"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\n  \"status\":\"complete\",\n  \"focus\":\"Read the two DSH route patches and compare their declarations.\",\n  \"findingsCount\":5,\n  \"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\n  \"noveltyJustification\":\"All five findings are new to this lineage, which had no prior research state.\",\n  \"keyQuestions\":[...4...],\n  \"answeredQuestions\":[...4...],\n  \"ruledOut\":[],\n  \"edgeCase\":\"none\",\n  \"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Bash\"],\n  \"sourcesQueried\":[...6...],\n  \"timestamp\":\"2026-11-06T16:02:xx.000Z\",\n  \"durationMs\":88000,\n  \"executor\":{\"kind\":\"cli-deepseek-harness\",\"model\":\"deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"max\",\"serviceTier\":null,\"sandboxMode\":\"workspace-write\",\"timeoutSeconds\":900}\n}\n```\n\nWait, `sandboxMode` for DSH config is null; but the invocation metadata says sandboxMode workspace-write. The executor config parser doesn't support sandboxMode for DSH (null). For the record provenance, use the invocation metadata values: kind, model, reasoningEffort, serviceTier, sandboxMode. This is provenance, not config. Fine.\n\n`durationMs`: compute from start 16:00:31 to now. Let me capture the write time in the Node script (`new Date().toISOString()`), and duration = now - Date.parse(\"2026-11-06T16:00:31.000Z\"). That will be ~90s. Good.\n\nFinding rows:\n```\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-001\",\"label\":\"...\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml\"]}\n```\nThe `label` should be the finding text, not too long. The prompt says the delta contains one finding row per finding with `label` text and `sources`. Use concise labels (the same finding statements, maybe shortened). Ensure the number of finding rows is 5.\n\nCould also add `graphEvents` nodes/edges. Not necessary; the verifier's graph count is 0 but markdown/delta counts 5, so it passes. The reducer's coverage graph may be empty, but convergence for 1 iteration is max cap. The prompt's graphEvents are optional. I'll omit to keep it clean.\n\nDelta file: line 1 iteration record, lines 2-6 finding rows. No trailing blank line? Fine.\n\nThen create the gateway event file `gateway-events/iter-001.json` with the same iteration record as a single object. The gateway event for a legacy-shaped iteration record: The prompt says hand the record to the gateway with fields `type: \"iteration\"`, etc. The gateway detects legacy-shaped rows and upcasts. It requires `runId`, `sessionId`, `lineageId`. Good. It will upcast to `deep_research.iteration_completed` and write. The gateway might also accept a canonical stem envelope; using the legacy row is exactly what the leaf contract says (`--event-json` holds the canonical iteration record). The YAML's note says the gateway accepts a legacy-shaped row and upcasts it. Good.\n\nOne concern: The gateway's upcast of a legacy iteration row uses `context.scope` from the event? It needs `iteration` from the row. It reads `record.iteration`. Good. It will map `status`, `newInfoRatio`, `ruledOut`; it drops findingsCount/focus etc. in the ledger, but the delta retains them.\n\nThe gateway event file must be a single JSON object. I'll write the same record.\n\nLet me write a Node script that:\n- Reads config for session ID.\n- Defines keyQuestions/answeredQuestions.\n- Builds the record with timestamp now and duration.\n- Writes `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` (iteration + 5 findings).\n- Writes `gateway-events/iter-001.json` (iteration record only).\n- Prints the record and counts.\n\nUse repo root cwd and the full lineage dir path. Let me do it."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_2EPZgMniFHf1L0pr0m3X4137","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"set -e\ncd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled\nLINEAGE=\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/013-dsh-live-contract-pin/research/fanout-live/lineages/dsh-live\"\nnode - \"$LINEAGE\" <<'EOF'\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst dir = process.argv[2];\nconst config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, 'deep-research-config.json'), 'utf8'));\nconst sessionId = config.lineage.sessionId;\nconst now = new Date();\nconst timestamp = now.toISOString();\nconst startedAt = '2026-11-06T16:00:31.000Z';\nconst durationMs = Math.max(0, now.getTime() - Date.parse(startedAt));\nconst keyQuestions = [\n  'What endpoint, model id, reasoning effort, and compat flags does `.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml` declare?',\n  'What endpoint, model id, reasoning effort, and compat flags does `.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml` declare?',\n  'Do the two route patches agree, and where do they differ?',\n  'Which route does the repository document as unverified pending a keyed run?',\n];\nconst sources = [\n  '.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml',\n  '.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml',\n  '.dsh/README.md',\n  '.dsh/SYNC.md',\n  'specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-llmgateway.txt',\n  'specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-opencode-go.txt',\n];\nconst record = {\n  type: 'iteration',\n  iteration: 1,\n  run: 1,\n  runId: sessionId,\n  sessionId,\n  lineageId: sessionId,\n  mode: 'research',\n  target_agent: 'deep-research',\n  agent_definition_loaded: true,\n  resolved_route: 'Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research',\n  status: 'complete',\n  focus: 'Read the two DSH route patches and compare their declarations.',\n  findingsCount: 5,\n  newInfoRatio: 1.0,\n  noveltyJustification: 'All five findings are new to this lineage, which had no prior research state.',\n  keyQuestions,\n  answeredQuestions: keyQuestions,\n  ruledOut: [],\n  edgeCase: 'none',\n  toolsUsed: ['Read', 'Bash'],\n  sourcesQueried: sources,\n  timestamp,\n  durationMs,\n  executor: {\n    kind: 'cli-deepseek-harness',\n    model: 'deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017',\n    reasoningEffort: 'max',\n    serviceTier: null,\n    sandboxMode: 'workspace-write',\n    timeoutSeconds: 900,\n  },\n};\nconst findings = [\n  {\n    id: 'f-iter001-001',\n    label: 'LLM Gateway patch: provider llmgateway, baseURL https://api.llmgateway.io/v1, api openai-completions, key LLMGATEWAY_API_KEY, model deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, default reasoningEffort max.',\n    sources: ['.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml'],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'f-iter001-002',\n    label: 'OpenCode Go patch: provider opencode-go, baseURL https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1, api openai-completions, key OPENCODE_API_KEY, model deepseek-v4.1-flash, default reasoningEffort max.',\n    sources: ['.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml'],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'f-iter001-003',\n    label: 'Both patches declare compat thinkingFormat deepseek and supportsDeveloperRole false, with the same off/high/max effort ladder and max as default.',\n    sources: ['.dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml', '.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml'],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'f-iter001-004',\n    label: 'They disagree on provider id, endpoint, key variable and exact model id; the OpenCode Go patch says its endpoint is unverified until a keyed run proves it.',\n    sources: ['.dsh/patches/route-opencode-go-deepseek.patch.yml', '.dsh/README.md'],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'f-iter001-005',\n    label: 'The patches are alternative pins, not additive: both target llm-pi-ai and agent-default-model, and the repository says a dispatch passes exactly one route patch.',\n    sources: ['.dsh/README.md', 'specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-llmgateway.txt', 'specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/004-dsh-runtime-folder-and-patches/evidence/dump-config-opencode-go.txt'],\n  },\n];\nconst deltaLines = [JSON.stringify(record), ...findings.map((finding) => JSON.stringify({\n  type: 'finding',\n  id: finding.id,\n  label: finding.label,\n  iteration: 1,\n  sources: finding.sources,\n}))];\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, 'deltas', 'iter-001.jsonl'), `${deltaLines.join('\\n')}\\n`, 'utf8');\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, 'gateway-events', 'iter-001.json'), JSON.stringify(record), 'utf8');\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ timestamp, durationMs, findingsCount: record.findingsCount, deltaLines: deltaLines.length, record }, null, 2));\nEOF","description":"Write iteration delta and gateway record"}}
