els its endpoint \"unverified until a keyed run proves it\"; the LLM Gateway patch carries no such caveat.\"\n\nWord count: Let me count roughly. ~150 words. Good.\n\nThe research.md can include a table of the declarations, the agreement/difference, and convergence report. It can be ~500 words total, but the answer is under 200. The task says \"answer in under 200 words\" — the Answer section satisfies.\n\nCitations:\n- `[SOURCE: .dsh/patches/route-llmgateway-deepseek.patch.yml:9]`\n- etc.\n\nThe synthesis closeout requires research.md exists before it runs. Good.\n\nLet me write research.md at the lineage root with the `write` tool. I'll include:\n- YAML frontmatter maybe.\n- `# DSH Route Patch Declarations`\n- `## Answer (under 200 words)`\n- `## 1. Research Question`\n- `## 2. Scope and Method`\n- `## 3. Declarations`\n- `## 4. Agreement`\n- `## 5. Differences`\n- `## 6. Verification Status`\n- `## 7. Evidence`\n- `## 8. Implications`\n- `## 9. Limitations`\n- `## 10. Recommendations`\n- `## 11. References`\n- `## Eliminated Alternatives` (table)\n- `## Divergence Map`\n- `## 12. Open Questions`\n- `## 13. Convergence Report`\n- `## 14. Scope and Workflow Notes`\n\nWait, if I put `## Eliminated Alternatives` after section 11 and before section 12, good. The Divergence Map after it. The convergence report can be after open questions. The 17-section template is less important than the mandatory sections.\n\nLet me ensure the `## Eliminated Alternatives` table includes the `ruledOut` entries (none) and dead ends (none). Use a row \"None — all four key questions were answered by direct file reading.\" That's fine.\n\nDivergence Map: saturated directions none, pivots none, remaining frontier none.\n\nScope and workflow notes: \"The auto-workflow's `step_writeback_spec_findings` and `phase_save` were not run because they write outside this lineage. The parent merge/operator owns them. No spec.md or continuity artifacts were modified.\" This documents the deviation.\n\n